# Shared Package Rules
# Pure TypeScript - No Framework Dependencies

## Purpose
- **Types, interfaces, enums** only - no runtime dependencies
- **Constants** - pure values, no side effects
- **Utility functions** - pure functions, no external deps
- **Shared between backend and frontend** - isomorphic code

## Constraints
- **No importing from backend or frontend**
- **No Node.js APIs** (fs, path, etc) - must work in browser
- **No React/NestJS imports** - framework agnostic
- **No database imports** - Prisma types only as type imports
- **No external dependencies** except TypeScript built-ins

## Code Style
- **Type-only imports** - `import type { ... }` for all cross-file imports
- **Interface over Type** - prefer `interface` for object shapes
- **Const enums** - for enums that should be inlined at compile time
- **Readonly arrays/objects** - use `readonly` keyword
- **Pure functions** - no side effects, deterministic output

## File Organization
```
src/
  ├── constants/     # Constant values
  │   ├── index.ts   # Export all constants
  │   └── pagination.ts
  ├── enums/         # Shared enums
  │   ├── index.ts
  │   └── status.ts
  ├── types/         # TypeScript interfaces/types
  │   ├── index.ts
  │   ├── user.ts
  │   └── api.ts
  ├── utils/         # Pure utility functions
  │   ├── index.ts
  │   └── formatting.ts
  └── index.ts       # Main export
```

## Testing
- **Unit tests only** - pure functions, no mocking needed
- **100% coverage goal** - small, testable functions
- **Property-based testing** - for complex utilities

## Build Output
- **CommonJS + ESM** dual output for maximum compatibility
- **Declaration files** (.d.ts) for TypeScript consumers
- **Source maps** for debugging
